cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use autocode, please cite it as below."
title: "AutoCode: 48 agent skills from a spoken request to a deployed URL"
abstract: >-
  AutoCode is a skill pack that takes a plain-language request through
  building, testing and deployment in a single session and returns a live URL.
  It ships 48 skills with no dependencies, installs into Claude Code, Codex,
  Hermes, Cursor and Gemini, uses the I-Lang v5.0 judgment layer to decide
  when to stop and ask, and keeps deployment secrets out of the model context.
type: software
